TO EDITOR OF NEUSLAND;

Your readers have been very much INTERESTED in the account given by your correspondents. Spotsylvania and Westmoreland of the admirable reply made by Gen. John Critcher in Congress to Hoar of Massachusetts, showing the utter falsity of his charge that slavery had demoralized the southerners, and defying him to show any portion of the whole country of the size of the county of Westmoreland that had produced as many such men as the Washingtons, Monroes, and the Lees.

The same charge made by Henry CABOT Lodge in a late number of the Cent., which you have ably repealed and answered in your issue of the 18th.

